this summer peter parker's returning to  the big screen in spider-man homecoming  the immensely popular character has been  through a lot over the last couple of  decades here's what's changed since the  webslinger first flew over the New York  skyline spider-man was introduced in  comics in 1962 and first popped up on  television in a short-lived CBS series  called The Amazing Spiderman in 1977 a  couple of films were released overseas  using footage that was recut from the TV  series after that a new spider-man movie  spent two decades and development have  multiple movie studios finally after a  legal battle between MGM and Sony over  rights to the character the two  companies settled and Sony went into  production in 2000 with Sam Raimi  directing and Tobey Maguire starring his  fight the first spider-man was released  in 2002 and was a critical and  commercial smash hit it was the first  movie ever to make over a hundred  million dollars in its opening weekend  it also helped pave the way for  superhero movies to take over Hollywood  the sequel  spider-man 2 was another critical in  box-office smash the franchise's woes  started to take hold in 2007 while  spider-man 3 was no box-office bomb it  fared poorly with critics and audiences  and the studio decided to cancel  spider-man for just five years later  Sony rebooted with the amazing  spider-man starring Andrew Garfield it  was another origin story but this time  they went back to spider-man's roots and  let him build his own web blasters which  was a nice touch reminding us all what a  genius the Peter Parker character is  supposed to be the follow-up the amazing  spider-man 2 was a critical and  commercial disappointment and Sony  quickly canceled plans for a third one  and also delayed plans for several  spider-man universe spin-offs including  the sinister six and venom with so many  other giant superhero blockbusters and  franchises things were looking rough for  spider but in an unprecedented deal  between Sony and Disney spider-man was  allowed to cross over into the Marvel  Cinematic Universe the new spy team  played by newcomer Tom Holland stole the  show in Captain America Civil War for  the first time it really felt like  spider-man was  like the teenager he is even better  Holland actually was a teenager when he  first donned the spandex suit as opposed  to Maguire and Garfield who were both in  their late twenties when they played the  role subgun wait a minute you guys are  the real Avengers I can tell hope gives  it away  spider-man homecoming looks and feels  more like a Marvel film than anything  Sony has done before  especially with the heavy use of Tony  Stark Stark design Spidey suit and it  looks like it's going to be full of Iron  Man like tricks and gadgets will  homecoming finally be a return to form  for the webslinger we'll find out in  July what do you think about the latest  spider-man trailer who's your favorite  spider-man let us know in the comments  below and don't forget to subscribe  [Music]
 

